    "buildMjsSha256": "f1ab1a243dc232ff855d5a4b1f4f23f70ec4204fc5d175400a33e2402528c202",
    "packageJsonSha256": "8e13ea99fbba085f8a05070ed4b0778f7c17aa9a5d8711d1cd5497f572d77364",
    "description": "build.mjs fetches the 49 site files from raw.githubusercontent.com (fallback: cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh) at the pinned commit 48cf269 and aborts unless each file byte length and SHA-256 match the values in `files` above, then writes them to ./public. The deployment therefore contains exactly the repo bytes of the pinned commit; this is the same pattern as the v20 and v20.1 deploys. The manifest was generated from the local checkout of 48cf269 (HEAD == origin/main, clean tree) and the script was dry-run locally (49/49 files byte-identical) before deploying. The build finished within about a minute; the raw deployment URL already served the verified v20.2 index on the first poll."
  },
  "notes": [
    "The repository is public (gh: visibility PUBLIC), which is what makes the pinned-commit fetch possible; the ~2.4 MB site tree (49 files, 2482517 B — the v20.2 avatar/splash PNGs and the redrawn PWA icons account for most of the growth from 665 KB) was therefore not inlined into the MCP request.",
    "Git-linked auto-deploy was not used, for the same reasons as before: create_git_project requires teamId (the 403 trigger) and cannot re-link the existing unlinked project proklinator-static.",
    "teamId was omitted from deploy_to_vercel, as in the prior successful deploys; no 403 occurred. Team-scoped read endpoints (get_deployment, get_deployment_build_logs) still return 404 for this token, so the build was followed and verified over HTTP against the raw deployment URL and the public alias.",
    "The existing project proklinator-static was reused (protection already off); no new project was created and no auth/SSO/protection settings were touched. Registration and payments were not opened.",
    "No app code was changed for this deploy; this commit updates DEPLOY_RESULT.json only.",
    "HUGINN was not touched."
  ]
}
